  "summary": "**Research run AR-20261030-02 — pending approval**\n\n**Universe & panel**: 29 housebuilders pass the ≥50% residential revenue screen (253 panel rows). Tsuchiya Holdings (1840, 土屋ホールディングス) is included with 100% residential share.\n\n**M1 equations**:  \n- P/B on 3-yr ROE (6.39), growth (−0.08), log revenue (0.01); n=253, residual scale 0.37.  \n- EV/EBITDA on 3-yr margin (−3.10), growth (0.72), log revenue (−0.08); n=214, scale 0.46.\n\n**Tsuchiya fitted multiples (2026 year effect)**: P/B 0.48 (0.30–0.77); EV/EBITDA 13.3 (7.4–23.9). Inputs: ROE 0.97%, growth −3.23%, margin 0.4%.\n\n**Annual backtest (9 non-overlapping years, 2016–2025)**: Only two methods meet the acceptance rule (mean IC > 0, t ≥ 2):  \n- M1 P/B regression: mean IC 0.12, t=2.13, top–bottom 1.7%, hit 52.2%.  \n- P/E peers (trailing): mean IC 0.14, t=2.88, top–bottom 9.9%, hit 52.5%.  \nAll other methods fail (negative/low IC or t < 2). Monthly reference (75–108 months) shows stronger IC and t for the same two methods.\n\n**Proposed weights**: M1 P/B 31.1%, P/E 33.2%, remaining five methods 7.1% each (½ equal + ½ by accepted IC).  \n\n**Weaknesses to note**: small universe (29 names); annual backtest only 9 observations; five of seven methods rejected; live P/E and EV/EBITDA use forward estimates while backtest uses trailing (no point-in-time forecast history); survivorship — panel requires price history.\n\n(Code check: 3 number(s) not found in the results and not verified: 20261030, 50%, 1840,)"
